+# «Оюун» online school assistant: report (15 November 2026)
+
+Branch `online-school` (on top of `chatbot-intelligence`). The demo business changed from the
+nail salon «Сувд» to the fictional online school «Оюун»: 1-on-1 live video lessons (English,
+IELTS and ЭЕШ preparation, maths and physics, programming, Korean/Chinese/Japanese) with six
+teachers. The assistant engine is unchanged in design; this report covers the switch. The salon
+report is in git history (`chatbot-intelligence`).
+
+## What changed in the assistant
+
+- **Vocabulary** (`salon/vocabulary.ts`): every course and teacher with Cyrillic, Latin-script
+  and English forms; generic words ask a choice («англи хэл» → which course, «математик» → which
+  grade); grades («7-р анги») are read as school bands, never as clock times; each thing the
+  school does not offer (music, German, chemistry, in-person or group classes, certificates,
+  beauty) gets its own honest reply.
+- **Dialogue copy**: багш, хичээл, сурагч, сургууль; lessons are online on Google Meet and the
+  link is sent after confirmation — in the demo nothing is sent, and the reply says so. A parent
+  may book for a child with the parent's name and phone. Add-on prices are shown; add-ons are
+  chosen on the booking page.
+- **Engine fixes** (shared, business-agnostic): a one-letter typo no longer matches a word with a
+  different first letter; a short word missing its last letter no longer matches; «хүүхэд» is no
+  longer a price question. Earlier the same day: next-week weekdays («ирэх 7 хоногийн мягмар»)
+  and more Latin-script spellings.
+- **Safety behaviour unchanged**: explicit yes before booking, reference + phone to see or change
+  a booking, hand-over, facts only from the database or verified knowledge.
+
+## Tests (exact results)
+
+| Command                                                            | Result                                                                    |
+| ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `npm run check` (lint, typecheck, unit + integration, build)       | exit 0; 259 tests (72 unit, 187 integration incl. 146 gate conversations) |
+| `playwright test` against the local dev server (desktop + Pixel 7) | 16/16                                                                     |
+| Held-out (new, written blind before the change), run once          | 111/135 turns (82.2%), 72/93 conversations; hard rules 135/135            |
+
+The held-out set was written from the school spec without reading the engine and committed before
+the assistant was changed. Nothing was tuned after its run. Misses
+([EVAL_HELDOUT_SCHOOL_RUN1.md](EVAL_HELDOUT_SCHOOL_RUN1.md)): five honest "not offered" replies
+worded differently than expected; hours questions in Latin script («davaa garagt hicheel ordog
+uu»); level-check and policy phrasings in Latin script; «minii hicheel hezee bilee» as a status
+question; "who am I talking to?"; a double QPay charge not handed over; an unknown teacher name
+ignored instead of corrected; a child's age not used to pick the kids' course; one conversation
+re-asking which English course. The next round fixes these, moves them to the gate and writes
+fresh held-out cases (see [EVALUATION.md](EVALUATION.md)).
+
+## Limitations
+
+- No live model run (no `OPENAI_API_KEY`); the model path is tested with fakes.
+- Add-ons are not chosen in the chat.
+- Booking references keep the `SV-` prefix (existing bookings and links use it).
+- Teacher coverage at weekends is one teacher per subject, so weekend alternatives are fewer.
+
+## Databases
+
+Only the throwaway embedded test databases and this worktree's local database
+(`127.0.0.1:54339`). Production was not touched; it still holds the salon catalogue, and switching
+the live demo needs a deliberate catalogue swap (see `docs/deployment.md`).
